From 02f52a863aa34baeb150c474da70b85d09982f8b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Denis Andreyev <257564291+unsound-mint@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 04:36:18 +0500
Subject: [PATCH 6/6] OpenMP in L-BFGS-B and BLAS (results independent of the
 thread count)

The loops of L-BFGS-B over all variables run in parallel: cauchy, cmprlb,
formk, subsm, projgr, the line-search update in lnsrlb, and ddot, dcopy,
daxpy and dscal in blas.f.

Sums over the variables are cut into blocks of nblk = 65536 elements
(omp_block.h). Each block is summed in index order and the block sums are
added in block order, so the result is the same for any number of threads
and with or without OpenMP. Up to 65536 variables there is one block and
every sum is the same as before; for more variables the order of the
additions changes, which changes results at the rounding level.

Loops that update one element per variable run in parallel as they are;
in cmprlb and subsm the loop over the variables is now the outer loop,
which keeps the order of the updates of each element. The breakpoint list
in cauchy, the step bound in lnsrlb and the backtracking in subsm stay
serial because their result depends on the order.
